      }
    },
    {
      "key": "lesson-11",
      "name": "Hyperparameters",
      "absolute_position": 11,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "overview": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-user-graduate\"></i> ***Career Journeys***\n\n**What decisions do I need to make about my machine learning model?**\n\nIn this lesson, students take on the role of game designers at a studio releasing a new video game: Lantern Deep. It’s up to students to optimize the studio’s classifiers. To do so, they learn about hyperparameters and how to tune them.",
        "preparation": "- Print copies of the Tuning Report Activity Guide (one for each student)",
        "student_overview": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-user-graduate\"></i> ***Career Journeys***\n\n**What decisions do I need to make about my machine learning model?**\n\nIn this lesson, you'll take on the role of a game designer at a studio releasing a new video game: Lantern Deep. It’s up to you to optimize the studio’s classifiers. To do so, you'll learn about hyperparameters and how to tune them."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "lesson-11",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "aif-year2-semester1-unit4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "lesson-12",
      "name": "Classification Project",
      "absolute_position": 12,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "overview": "In this lesson, students choose a classification problem and build a classifier to solve it. They explore the shape of their chosen problem, using their findings to inform their choice of classifier: either a nearest-neighbors classifier or a decision tree. Students then build their chosen classifier: they encode features, split their data, and fit their model. Finally, students evaluate their model using metrics of their choice and optimize its performance for those metrics. Throughout the project, students reflect on their design decisions in their Project Planning Guide.",
        "preparation": "- Print one copy of the Classification Project Planning Guide for each student.",
        "student_overview": "In this lesson, you'll choose a classification problem and build a classifier to solve it."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "lesson-12",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "aif-year2-semester1-unit4"
      }
    }
  ],
